/*! \page settings Environment settings reference

Every environment variable the library reads, grouped by what it is for.  **A setting is not the same as a diagnostic**: a
*setting* changes how or what is computed (or the resources used); a *diagnostic* only prints or records something.
`scripts/audit-settings-doc` (a ctest) fails if the code reads a name that is missing from this page.

\section settings_tiers How to read the tables
- **Default** — what you get with the variable unset.  *Moves numbers?* — **no** (output or timing only), **~ulp** (bit-level,
  below ~1e-12) or **yes** (changes a converged value or the trajectory).
- A name followed by *(alias GPW_…)* is the **renamed** form; the old `GPW_` name still works and prints a one-time
  deprecation notice (\ref qchem::Env).  The `GPW_` prefix is kept only for settings specific to the Gaussian-plane-wave basis.
- These are being replaced by typed options in the run description (D-ENV, `doc/CleanCode.md`); until then this page is the reference.

\section settings_resources Resources — never change a number

| setting | default | what it does |
|---|---|---|
| `QCHEM_OPENMP_THREADS` *(alias `GPW_OMP_THREADS`)* | 1 (serial) | OpenMP worker count for **every** region we own (pair loops, XC-mesh tables and quadrature, the Becke-mesh build, seed and FT sampling).  `0` = auto = the number of **physical** cores; `N` = N; invalid = 1.  See \ref qchem::WorkerThreads. |
| `QCHEM_BLAS_THREADS` | 1 | BLAS/LAPACK threads (OpenBLAS).  Deliberately separate: N BLAS threads inside N OpenMP threads is a measured net loss, and the run banner warns if both exceed 1.  See \ref qchem::BlasThreads. |
| `OMP_NUM_THREADS`, `KMP_BLOCKTIME` | — | Standard OpenMP variables; only read to describe the run on the banner (`KMP_BLOCKTIME`/`OMP_WAIT_POLICY` are *set* to non-spinning defaults by \ref qchem::StopOmpThreadsBusyWaiting unless you set them). |
| `GPW_COLLOC_MEMO` | 4 | Depth of the density-collocation replay cache (memory against time). |

\section settings_policy Declared deviations and the CP2K umbrella — NOW DECK KEYS (the environment variables are retired)

Resolved once per run (\ref qchem::RunPolicy, from \c SolidCalcOptions::policy) and printed on the run banner with a `*` where the run deviates
from CP2K parity.  `policy.cp2kCompat=true` sets every route to CP2K's choice; stating a route explicitly outranks the umbrella.  The environment
variables below are **retired and ignored** (reported once, recorded in `provenance.ignoredEnvironment`); set one with
`--set solid.policy.<key>=<value>`.

| retired variable | deck key | default | what it does |
|---|---|---|---|
| `CP2K_COMPAT` | `policy.cp2kCompat` | false | Umbrella: run at CP2K parity (also forces symmetry imposition off). |
| `QCHEM_DM_LOWRANK` | `policy.dmLowRank` | on | Factored/low-rank ρ route (a singles route CP2K does not run). |
| `GPW_STREAM_FOLD` | `policy.streamFold` | on | Orbit fold of the GPW collocation pair streams. |
| `QCHEM_MIX_RHO_M` | `policy.mixRhoM` | on | Mix in (ρ, m) channels (Kerker on ρ, linear on m) instead of (↑, ↓). |
| `QCHEM_XC_DM_SOURCE` (`GPW_XC_DM_SOURCE`) | `policy.xcFromDM` | off | Feed V_xc the wholesale ρ[D] instead of the mixed ρ. |
| `QCHEM_IMPOSE_SYMMETRY` | `policy.imposeSymmetry` | on | Whether the caller may impose space-group symmetry at all. |
| `QCHEM_BECKE_XC` | `policy.beckeXC` | on | Atom-centred (Becke) XC quadrature rather than the uniform grid. |
| `GPW_DAWARE_SCREEN` | `policy.dAwareScreen` | on | D-aware collocation box tolerance ε/\|c_ij\| instead of a flat ε. |
| `QCHEM_U_EIGEN` | `policy.hubbardEigen` | on | DFT+U on the Löwdin block's eigenvalues (Dudarev) instead of its diagonal populations. |

\section settings_numerics Numerical-method tolerances and grids — NOW DECK KEYS (the environment variables are retired)

These moved numbers, so they are part of a run's input and live in the input deck (\c solid.tolerances.*, \c solid.xcMesh.*), where they are
reproducible from the run's numbered revision file.  The environment variables below are **retired and ignored**: each is reported once on
stderr with its replacement, and recorded in the run's \c provenance.ignoredEnvironment.  Set one with \c --set \<deck key\>=\<value\>.

| retired variable | deck key | default | what it does |
|---|---|---|---|
| `GPW_DENSITY_EPS` | `solid.tolerances.densityEps` | 1e-10 | Screening tolerance for the collocated density (sizes the shell-pair/offset task list). |
| `GPW_SCREEN_EPS` | `solid.tolerances.screenEps` | 1e-10 | Magnitude screen for the analytic lattice sums (CP2K `EPS_PGF_ORB` analogue). |
| `GPW_VLOC_EPS` | `solid.tolerances.vlocEps` | 1e-5 | Tolerance of the local-pseudopotential long-range G-ball. |
| `GPW_FIELDSHARP` | `solid.tolerances.fieldSharp` | 2/3 | κ: the KS field's core exponent as a fraction of α_max. |
| `GPW_RELFIELDSHARP` | `solid.tolerances.relFieldSharp` | 1/3 | The HartreeOnly floor, as a fraction of α_max (β = 0 diverges). |
| `GPW_LOCALPP_RELCUTOFF` | `solid.tolerances.localPPRelCutoff` | 30 Ha | Absolute pair→level rule κ for the local-PP sweeps. |
| `GPW_MGRID_ECUTS` | `solid.tolerances.mgridEcuts` | — | Explicit multigrid cutoff list (Ha, descending) — for matching CP2K's `CUTOFF/3^i`. |
| `GPW_RELCUTOFF` | `solid.tolerances.relCutoff` | 0 | Force the absolute pair→level rule at this κ (Ha) — the CP2K-matching experiment. |
| `QCHEM_BECKE_NR` (`GPW_BECKE_NR`) | `solid.xcMesh.nRadial` | 40 | Becke XC mesh: radial points. |
| `QCHEM_BECKE_ALPHA` (`GPW_BECKE_ALPHA`) | `solid.xcMesh.mhlAlpha` | 2.0 | Becke XC mesh: MHL radial scale. |
| `QCHEM_BECKE_L` (`GPW_BECKE_L`) | `solid.xcMesh.angularDegree` | 29 | Becke XC mesh: angular polynomial degree. |
| `QCHEM_BECKE_ROT` (`GPW_BECKE_ROT`) | `solid.xcMesh.angRot` | 0 | Becke XC mesh: rigid rotation of the angular grid (radians). |
| `QCHEM_BECKE_EPS` (`GPW_BECKE_EPS`) | `solid.xcMesh.beckeEps` | 1e-6 | Becke competitor-series tolerance. |

The controls of the XC-from-D route moved with it, into the same `policy` block (retired variables, deck keys):

| retired variable | deck key | default | what it does |
|---|---|---|---|
| `QCHEM_XC_DM_MIX` (`GPW_XC_DM_MIX`) | `policy.xcDMMix` | unset | Override the XC-from-D mixing α (1 = the undamped route; unset = the mixer's own). Only used when `policy.xcFromDM` is on. |
| `QCHEM_XC_DM_BOOST` (`GPW_XC_DM_BOOST`) | `policy.xcDMBoost` | 1 | Scale that α. |

\section settings_hatches A/B hatches — REMOVED (D-ENV 6c)

These were verification switches between two routes that agree (to ~ulp, or to the screen).  They are **retired and ignored** (reported once with
"removed"): the route they selected is the default.  The A/B survives as a unit-test hook where a test needs it
(`NR_Evaluator::ContractCubeOverride`, `ExpRecurrenceOverride`, `SphereScreenOverride`); it is not a run input, so it is not in the deck.

| retired variable | what it switched |
|---|---|
| `GPW_CONTRACT_CUBE` | `=0` the reference box walk instead of the separable contraction (agree to ~1e-14). |
| `GPW_EXP_RECURRENCE` | exp recurrence vs direct evaluation (~ulp). |
| `GPW_SPHERE_SCREEN` | spherical vs rectangular-hull log-cut in the collocation. |
| `GPW_LONG_SWEEP` | the old long-range local-PP kappa sweep, for A/B against the custom G-ball (a non-Gaussian local model still falls back to it). |

\section settings_diag Diagnostics — print or record only; never change a number

Switch on with `QCHEM_DIAGNOSTICS=id[=value],...`; `QCHEM_DIAGNOSTICS=list` prints the registry.  The old name in the second
column still works (on unless `0`; its value is the argument).  A mistyped id warns.  Source of truth: \ref qchem::Diagnostics::Registry.

| id | old name | what it prints |
|---|---|---|
| `becke_atoms` | `GPW_BECKE_ATOMS` | per-atom Becke share / kept / dropped breakdown |
| `becke_count` | `GPW_BECKE_COUNT` | census of Becke per-point partition costs |
| `dm_rank` | `GPW_DM_RANK` | rank / PSD census of D and the IPR of its Cholesky orbitals |
| `eh_trace` | `GPW_EH_TRACE` | E_H G-space pairing trace |
| `field_spectrum` | `GPW_FIELD_SPECTRUM` | cumulative \|c\|² spectrum of a fitted field |
| `gdm_trace` | `GPW_GDMTRACE` | GDM line-search energy trace |
| `integrate_census` | `GPW_INTEGRATE_CENSUS` | NEW / REPEAT census of integrate-back calls |
| `kerker_spectrum` | `GPW_KERKER_SPECTRUM` | Kerker residual power binned by G/G0 |
| `localpp_timing` | — | times the local-PP build |
| `mesh_ortho` | `GPW_MESH_ORTHO` | plane-wave orthogonality error of the XC mesh binned in \|ΔG\|; value = half-width of the ΔG box (default 1, use 4) |
| `metal_trace` | `GPW_METALTRACE` | shared-μ fill, per-block trace |
| `nl_per_l` | `GPW_NL_PER_L` | bank the per-l non-local projector blocks |
| `phi_sparsity` | `GPW_PHI_SPARSITY` | block-sparsity ceiling of the Φ table |
| `rho_negative` | `GPW_RHO_NEGATIVE` | negative-ρ census per XC route |
| `rss_trace` | `GPW_RSS_TRACE` | resident-memory breadcrumbs in the lattice sum |
| `xc_alpha` | `GPW_XC_ALPHA` | the XC mix's effective α each step |
| `xc_route` | `GPW_XCROUTE` | which V_xc route fires each iteration |
| `angmesh_debug` | `QCHEM_ANGMESH_DEBUG` | NNLS site-adapted angular-mesh debug print |
| `dump_h` | `QCHEM_DUMP_H` | ‖F‖, trace and max imaginary part of each Hamiltonian |
| `mom_scores` | `QCHEM_MOM_SCORES` | sorted head of the MOM scores at each fill |
| `u_trace` | `QCHEM_U_TRACE` | per-refresh +U occupation line on stdout |

Integrated site moments are no longer a diagnostic: a polarized run prints them in its result line.

\section settings_drivers Test and probe drivers (not the library)

The integration-test harness (`EnvOverrides`: `GPW_MEASURE`, `GPW_EPS`, `GPW_NMAX`, `GPW_PULAY`, `GPW_PULAY_START`, `GPW_MOM`, `GPW_ACC`,
`GPW_KERKER_G0`, `GPW_IMPOSE`, `GPW_ORTHO`, `GPW_REAL`, `GPW_SEED`, `GPW_SMEAR`, `GPW_VERBOSE`) and `gpwprobe` (the `<P>_*` variables,
`MNO_*`, `NIO_*`) read the environment as a crude input deck.  They are documented in `doc/Records/EnvKnobInventory.md` §4 and
are to be replaced by the input deck (D-ENV step 6).
*/
